item.text:
{
  "approved": false,
  "issues": [
    "Incomplete security answers can reach verify_identity: the pre-hook sends a two-digit phone answer unchanged, and an existing check explicitly accepts that request. Because a pre-hook cannot cancel an action, completeness must be checked before exposing the verification call.",
    "Returning to identity after callback clarification can produce no speech because its only entry action is first-entry-only TTS. Security staging also needs a speaking return path.",
    "The decision code can lose a proposed date when offering the floor, subsequently recording the old offer date after acceptance. It also fails to update current_index when a customer selects another product, allowing the next acceptance to affect the wrong product.",
    "An initial all-products affordability rejection offers the first floor without starting that product at attempt 1 and its prescribed date, contrary to B4. A combined monetary total can also be copied independently to every product.",
    "The payment parser treats every unparsed exact date as a vague period, potentially replacing it with the deadline after two clarifications. It additionally imports the DOB-only numeric day/month rule into payment and callback dates.",
    "The confirmation node cannot extract paid, dispute, too_much, or a voluntary payment proposal accompanying hardship. Declining support can leave earlier, unrecorded promises pending and return to confirmation instead of resolving them as hardship.",
    "resolution_ready remains yes after reconciliation. Returning from finalization to record can therefore immediately leave again before a requested transfer or correction is handled. The existing return transition also does not capture and validate the interrupting correction.",
    "When a final promise fails twice after another product succeeded, routing bypasses the failure instruction and reconciliation only mentions successful promises. The customer is not reliably told which promise could not be recorded.",
    "A failed duplicate write can downgrade a previously recorded product to service_error. Successful recorded state must remain authoritative.",
    "A lookup failure reaches finalize, which has neither get_account nor a retry transition, despite the policy promising a customer-requested repeat after a confirmed API 500.",
    "The security post-hook counts an ok=true response with a missing verified field as a wrong answer. An incomplete response is not evidence of an actual wrong answer."
  ],
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/policy/identity/assembly",
      "value": "Use the corrected part of an utterance; assemble fragments across turns and preserve leading zeroes. A code step checks completeness before the verification tool is exposed. Partial, ambiguous, superseded or month-word-hint-incompatible answers cause clarification without a bank call or a consumed attempt."
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/policy/calendar/numeric_payment_dates",
      "value": "The mandatory numeric day/month/year interpretation applies to DOB. For ambiguous numeric payment or callback dates, ask for the month as a word rather than inventing a bank interpretation. Do not count an exact but ambiguous date as a vague period."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/policy/calendar/weekend_gap",
      "value": "If now falls after the last business day of its calendar week, including on a Friday holiday, the literal attempt-1 date is past. The brief supplies no replacement rule. Do not offer or record that past date; ask for a permissible exact day without inventing a replacement persuasion date."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/policy/amounts/above_full",
      "value": "The supplied acceptance range ends at past_due. Re-offer the full past_due and obtain agreement; do not silently reduce a proposal or invent a separate bank overpayment policy."
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/test_variables/security_answer",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/test_variables/security_need_month_word",
      "value": "no"
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/test_variables/security_result_state",
      "value": "idle"
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/test_variables/amount_scope",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/test_variables/finalization_started",
      "value": "no"
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/test_variables/account_retry_permitted",
      "value": "no"
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/on_enter",
      "value": {
        "type": "llm",
        "prompt": "If the opening has not yet been spoken, say exactly: I am a digital assistant calling from Freya Bank, and this call is recorded. Am I speaking with {{title}} {{last_name}}? Otherwise immediately follow the current identity feedback without repeating the opening: {{identity_feedback}}. Ask only the missing callback/security detail or the next unpassed security question. Security stage: {{security_state}}."
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/on_enter_first_entry_only",
      "value": false
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/tools",
      "value": [
        "transfer_to_agent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/task_message",
      "value": "Establish that the speaker is the named customer. Only yes, that's me, speaking or their own name confirms. Hello/go ahead/who is this does not. Ask the name question at most twice total, answering their question first. If still unclear, finish as unclear. Never reveal the purpose or accounts here.\nIf someone else answers, ask when the customer can be reached. Relatives cannot answer security or receive account details even if offering to pay. Wrong number finishes wrong_number. For death say exactly 'I am sorry for your loss.' and ask nothing else. A third party unable to provide a callback finishes no_callback. Gather callback date and time without scheduling an unvalidated proposal.\nImmediately follow validation feedback: {{identity_feedback}}. For a confirmed customer ask DOB first, then phone last four only after DOB passed. Security stage: {{security_state}}. Gather only customer-supplied answers. Use the final corrected answer, assemble split answers across turns, retain leading zeroes, and ask only for missing pieces. A partial answer or correction is never a refusal or a wrong attempt. Complete answers are validated before checking them with the bank; do not claim they passed merely because they are complete. Purely numeric DOB means day/month/year. A swapped-day/month hint requires the customer to say the month as a word. Never re-ask a passed question. After three actual wrong answers, direct the customer to the mobile app or a branch and disclose no debt.\nFor a security refusal or a question about the call's purpose instead of an answer, explain once that the questions protect their account. The second refusal/purpose question finishes declined. Two statements not wanting to talk also finish declined.\nFor AI questions identify yourself as Freya Bank's digital assistant. For scam concerns say they can verify by calling Freya Bank's customer service number; do not invent the number. For a human request ask once whether you can help first; if they insist CALL transfer_to_agent with general. This is the only bank tool available here. Never ask a third party security questions. After any result speak or perform the next permitted action immediately. A failed transfer is not a connection."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/extraction_schema/1/enum_values",
      "value": [
        "",
        "callback",
        "security"
      ]
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/extraction_schema/1/description",
      "value": "security when the confirmed named customer supplies or corrects any part of the security answer currently requested, including incomplete fragments. callback only for a known third party supplying or completing callback details. Never interpret a security date as a callback or a name confirmation as a security answer. Otherwise empty."
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/extraction_schema/-",
      "value": {
        "name": "security_answer",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The customer's final corrected answer to the current security question, assembling only their supplied pieces across turns. For phone digits retain leading zeroes and include all digits supplied for this answer. For DOB normalize spoken day/year numbers, retaining a spoken month as a word; preserve purely numeric source order as DD/MM/YYYY. Do not invent missing day, month, year or digits. A correction replaces the superseded portion. Never copy a previous failed answer when the customer is supplying a new one.",
        "min_confidence": 0.7
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/transitions/2/condition/conditions/-",
      "value": {
        "variable": "event",
        "operator": "equals",
        "operand": "security"
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/identity/transitions/2/description",
      "value": "Validate a customer-supplied security answer or third-party callback before exposing its bank action."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/collect/extraction_schema/0/description",
      "value": "Latest substantive response only. accept agrees to the current explicit offer, including the initial all-products offer. proposal includes every volunteered amount/date, even invalid or vague, and a voluntary proposal accompanying hardship; never classify these as refusal. too_much explicitly says the full amount is too much. refuse includes flat no/non-answer or rejection of the floor/deadline but excludes clarification, questions and alternative proposals. paid means this past-due amount was paid; historical payoff/closure is dispute. hardship applies to illness, family death or job loss without a voluntary proposal, including when accompanied by a restructuring request. decline_support requires rejection of an actual support offer. no_talk is an explicit wish not to talk. Human requests and support acceptance remain empty for dialogue to handle. Otherwise empty."
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/collect/extraction_schema/3/description",
      "value": "Final corrected payment-date expression. Normalize unambiguous spoken day/year numbers, preserving a named month, but retain today/tomorrow and this/next weekday literally for code to interpret from call now. Preserve ambiguous purely numeric source dates rather than choosing their order. Do not invent missing components, use the real clock, or extract a small-talk date. Empty when no payment date is proposed."
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/collect/extraction_schema/-",
      "value": {
        "name": "amount_scope",
        "type": "string",
        "enum_values": [
          "",
          "per_product",
          "combined"
        ],
        "description": "per_product only when the customer expressly assigns the proposed amount to the identified single product or says this same amount for EACH identified product. combined for a total across products. Empty when unspecified. Never infer an allocation.",
        "min_confidence": 0.7
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/workflow/nodes/decide/code",
      "value": "import json, re, datetime\nevent = ''\ntry:\n    event = str(vars.get('event', ''))\n    scope = str(vars.get('scope', 'current'))\n    amount_text = str(vars.get('amount_text', '')).strip()\n    amount_scope = str(vars.get('amount_scope', ''))\n    phrase = str(vars.get('date_phrase', '')).strip()\n    security_answer = str(vars.get('security_answer', '')).strip()\n    cb_time = str(vars.get('callback_time', '')).strip()\n    hardship = vars.get('hardship_mentioned') == 'yes'\n    initial_offer = vars.get('split_started') != 'yes'\n    vars['event'] = ''\n    vars['amount_text'] = ''\n    vars['amount_scope'] = ''\n    vars['date_phrase'] = ''\n    vars['hardship_mentioned'] = 'no'\n    vars['decision_route'] = 'collect'\n    vars['next_instruction'] = 'Ask only for the missing or unclear payment detail.'\n    vars['identity_feedback'] = ''\n    vars['resolution_ready'] = 'no'\n    vars['close_ready'] = 'no'\n    if event != 'confirm':\n        vars['confirmation_state'] = 'none'\n        vars['confirmed_promises'] = []\n    now = datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(str(vars.get('now', '')).replace('Z', '+00:00')).replace(tzinfo=None)\n    today = now.date()\n    holidays = ['2026-10-26', '2026-11-11', '2026-11-26', '2026-12-25', '2027-01-01']\n    def business(d):\n        return d.weekday() < 5 and d.isoformat() not in holidays\n    def following(d):\n        while not business(d):\n            d += datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n        return d\n    def parsed(text):\n        try:\n            text = text.lower().strip().replace(',', '')\n            text = re.sub(r'^on\\s+', '', text)\n            if text == 'today':\n                return today\n            if text == 'tomorrow':\n                return today + datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n            if text in ['day after tomorrow', 'the day after tomorrow']:\n                return today + datetime.timedelta(days=2)\n            days = ['monday', 'tuesday', 'wednesday', 'thursday', 'friday', 'saturday', 'sunday']\n            m = re.fullmatch(r'(this|next)\\s+(monday|tuesday|wednesday|thursday|friday|saturday|sunday)', text)\n            if m:\n                monday = today - datetime.timedelta(days=today.weekday())\n                return monday + datetime.timedelta(days=days.index(m.group(2)) + (7 if m.group(1) == 'next' else 0))\n            if re.fullmatch(r'\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}', text):\n                return datetime.date.fromisoformat(text)\n            clean = re.sub(r'(\\d)(st|nd|rd|th)\\b', r'\\1', text)\n            clean = re.sub(r'\\b(the|of)\\s+', '', clean)\n            for fmt in ['%d %B %Y', '%B %d %Y', '%d %b %Y', '%b %d %Y', '%d %B', '%B %d', '%d %b', '%b %d']:\n                try:\n                    p = datetime.datetime.strptime(clean, fmt)\n                    return datetime.date(p.year if '%Y' in fmt else today.year, p.month, p.day)\n                except Exception:\n                    pass\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        return False\n    if vars.get('transfer_requested') == 'yes':\n        vars['decision_route'] = 'reconcile' if vars.get('transfer_state') == 'succeeded' else 'record'\n        vars['record_mode'] = 'transfer_hold'\n        vars['next_instruction'] = 'The requested transfer must be resolved. Do not negotiate, record abandoned promises or write notes. Do not repeat a successful transfer. A failed transfer may be repeated on customer request after a confirmed API 500.'\n    elif event == 'security':\n        vars['decision_route'] = 'identity'\n        vars['record_mode'] = ''\n        vars['pending_facts'] = ''\n        vars['security_result_state'] = 'idle'\n        stage = str(vars.get('security_state', 'date_of_birth'))\n        answer = ''\n        if stage == 'failed':\n            vars['decision_route'] = 'reconcile'\n        elif stage == 'verified':\n            vars['identity_feedback'] = 'Security is already complete. Do not re-ask either passed question.'\n        elif stage == 'date_of_birth' and vars.get('dob_passed') != 'yes':\n            month_word = bool(re.search(r'\\b(january|february|march|april|may|june|july|august|september|october|november|december|jan|feb|mar|apr|jun|jul|aug|sep|sept|oct|nov|dec)\\b', security_answer.lower()))\n            if vars.get('security_need_month_word') == 'yes' and not month_word:\n                vars['identity_feedback'] = 'Ask the customer to say the birth month as a word. Do not submit a numeric-only retry or count an attempt.'\n            else:\n                clean = re.sub(r'(\\d)(st|nd|rd|th)\\b', r'\\1', security_answer.lower().replace(',', ''))\n                m = re.fullmatch(r'(\\d{1,2})[/.\\-](\\d{1,2})[/.\\-](\\d{4})', clean)\n                try:\n                    if m:\n                        answer = datetime.date(int(m.group(3)), int(m.group(2)), int(m.group(1))).isoformat()\n                    else:\n                        for fmt in ['%Y-%m-%d', '%d %B %Y', '%B %d %Y', '%d %b %Y', '%b %d %Y']:\n                            try:\n                                answer = datetime.datetime.strptime(clean, fmt).date().isoformat()\n                                break\n                            except Exception:\n                                pass\n                except Exception:\n                    answer = ''\n                if not answer:\n                    vars['identity_feedback'] = 'Ask only for the missing or ambiguous part of the birth date, including the year if missing. Use the corrected customer answer. Do not validate a partial answer or count an attempt.'\n        elif stage == 'phone_last4' and vars.get('dob_passed') == 'yes' and vars.get('phone_passed') != 'yes':\n            words = dict(zero='0', oh='0', one='1', two='2', three='3', four='4', five='5', six='6', seven='7', eight='8', nine='9')\n            candidate = ''.join(words.get(x, x) for x in re.split(r'[\\s,\\-]+', security_answer.lower()))\n            if re.fullmatch(r'\\d{4}', candidate):\n                answer = candidate\n            else:\n                vars['identity_feedback'] = 'Ask only for the missing or unclear phone digits, preserving the digits already supplied and leading zeroes. Do not submit fewer or more than four digits, pad an answer, or count an attempt.'\n        else:\n            vars['identity_feedback'] = 'Do not re-ask a passed question. Explain that complete bank verification has not yet been confirmed; disclose no account information.'\n        if answer:\n            vars['prepared_security_field'] = stage\n            vars['prepared_security_answer'] = answer\n            vars['security_result_state'] = 'awaiting'\n            vars['record_mode'] = 'security'\n            vars['pending_facts'] = json.dumps(dict(field=stage, answer=answer))\n            vars['next_instruction'] = 'Immediately check this complete customer-supplied answer with verify_identity. Do not claim verification before its result.'\n            vars['decision_route'] = 'record'\n    elif event == 'callback':\n        vars['decision_route'] = 'identity'\n        next_day = following(today + datetime.timedelta(days=1))\n        vars['callback_facts'] = json.dumps(dict(today=today.isoformat(), next_business_day=next_day.isoformat(), earliest='10:00', latest='19:00', strictly_after=str(vars.get('now', ''))))\n        date_text = phrase or str(vars.get('callback_draft_phrase', ''))\n        time_text = cb_time or str(vars.get('callback_draft_time', ''))\n        vars['callback_draft_phrase'] = date_text\n        vars['callback_draft_time'] = time_text\n        d = parsed(date_text) if date_text else False\n        time_match = re.fullmatch(r'(\\d{2}):(\\d{2})', time_text)\n        t = False\n        if time_match:\n            try:\n                t = datetime.time(int(time_match.group(1)), int(time_match.group(2)))\n            except Exception:\n                pass\n        invalid = bool(d and d not in [today, next_day]) or bool(t and not datetime.time(10, 0) <= t <= datetime.time(19, 0)) or bool(time_match and not t)\n        if re.fullmatch(r'\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}', date_text) and not d:\n            invalid = True\n        if d and t and datetime.datetime.combine(d, t) <= now:\n            invalid = True\n        if invalid:\n            count = int(vars.get('callback_invalid_count', 0)) + 1\n            vars['callback_invalid_count'] = count\n            vars['callback_draft_phrase'] = ''\n            vars['callback_draft_time'] = ''\n            vars['callback_time'] = ''\n            if count >= 2:\n                vars['identity_exit'] = 'no_callback'\n                vars['decision_route'] = 'reconcile'\n            else:\n                vars['identity_feedback'] = 'That time is outside the callback window. Ask once for another time: today ' + today.isoformat() + ' or ' + next_day.isoformat() + ', 10:00 through 19:00, strictly later than the call time.'\n        elif not d or not t:\n            vars['identity_feedback'] = 'Ask only for the missing or ambiguous callback day or time; ask for a named month if a numeric date is ambiguous. Allowed days: ' + today.isoformat() + ' and ' + next_day.isoformat() + '; 10:00–19:00, later than now. Do not schedule yet.'\n        else:\n            vars['callback_date_ready'] = d.isoformat()\n            vars['callback_time_ready'] = t.strftime('%H:%M')\n            vars['callback_state'] = 'ready'\n            vars['record_mode'] = 'callback'\n            vars['pending_facts'] = json.dumps(dict(date=d.isoformat(), time=t.strftime('%H:%M')))\n            vars['next_instruction'] = 'Immediately schedule exactly the validated callback date and time.'\n            vars['decision_route'] = 'record'\n    else:\n        rows = vars.get('product_state', [])\n        if isinstance(rows, str):\n            rows = json.loads(rows)\n        if not isinstance(rows, list) or not rows or vars.get('security_state') != 'verified':\n            raise ValueError('Missing verified products')\n        vars['operational_hold'] = ''\n        current = int(vars.get('current_index', 0))\n        if not 0 <= current < len(rows):\n            current = 0\n        targets = [p for p in rows if p.get('state') in ['open', 'pending']] if scope == 'all' else [p for p in rows if p.get('product_id') == (rows[current]['product_id'] if scope == 'current' else scope)]\n        if targets:\n            current = next(i for i, p in enumerate(rows) if p['product_id'] == targets[0]['product_id'])\n            vars['current_index'] = current\n        messages = []\n        blocked = False\n        if hardship:\n            vars['hardship_active'] = 'yes'\n            messages.append('Give one short sentence of sympathy and offer connection to customer support. Process a voluntary payment proposal without persuasion.')\n        def signature(amount, date):\n            return str(float(amount)) + '|' + str(date)\n        def offer(p):\n            if vars.get('hardship_active') == 'yes':\n                return 'Offer connection to customer support; do not persuade.'\n            while int(p.get('attempts', 0)) < int(p['attempt_limit']):\n                n = int(p.get('attempts', 0)) + 1\n                p['attempts'] = n\n                a = p['floor'] if n == 2 or p.get('full_too_much') else p['past_due']\n                d = p['deadline'] if n == 2 else p['attempt1_date']\n                if not d:\n                    p['offer_amount'] = a\n                    p['offer_date'] = ''\n                    return 'The literal attempt-1 day is past and cannot be offered. Ask for an exact permissible payment day; allowed days are ' + ', '.join(p['allowed_dates']) + '.'\n                if signature(a, d) in p.get('rejected', []):\n                    continue\n                p['offer_amount'] = a\n                p['offer_date'] = d\n                p['amount'] = a\n                p['date'] = ''\n                return 'Offer ' + p['label'] + ': ' + str(a) + ' on ' + d + '.' + (' Explain that the rest stays overdue.' if a < p['past_due'] else '')\n            p['state'] = 'note'\n            p['reason'] = 'refused'\n            return ''\n        if event == 'confirm':\n            pending = [p for p in rows if p.get('state') == 'pending']\n            if vars.get('confirmation_state') != 'awaiting' or not pending or any(p.get('state') == 'open' for p in rows):\n                messages.append('A complete current joint read-back is required before confirmation.')\n                blocked = True\n            else:\n                if not all(p['date'] in p['allowed_dates'] and p['floor'] <= float(p['amount']) <= p['past_due'] for p in pending):\n                    raise ValueError('Invalid confirmed proposal')\n                vars['confirmation_state'] = 'confirmed'\n                vars['confirmed_promises'] = [dict(product_id=p['product_id'], amount=p['amount'], date=p['date']) for p in pending]\n                vars['record_mode'] = 'promises'\n                vars['decision_route'] = 'record'\n                messages.append('Immediately call create_promise for the first still-pending confirmed product.')\n        elif event == 'no_talk':\n            count = int(vars.get('dont_talk_count', 0)) + 1\n            vars['dont_talk_count'] = count\n            if count >= 2:\n                for p in rows:\n                    if p.get('state') in ['open', 'pending']:\n                        p['state'] = 'note'\n                        p['reason'] = 'refused'\n            else:\n                messages.append('Acknowledge briefly that they do not want to talk. Do not treat this as a second refusal; keep the next question short.')\n                blocked = True\n        elif event in ['hardship', 'decline_support']:\n            vars['hardship_active'] = 'yes'\n            if event == 'hardship':\n                if not hardship:\n                    messages.append('Say one short sentence of sympathy and offer connection to customer support. Make no persuasion attempt.')\n                blocked = True\n            else:\n                for p in rows:\n                    if p.get('state') == 'open' or p.get('state') == 'pending' and not p.get('voluntary_hardship'):\n                        p['state'] = 'note'\n                        p['reason'] = 'hardship'\n                        p['date'] = ''\n        elif event in ['paid', 'dispute']:\n            if not targets:\n                messages.append('Clarify which actual product this concerns.')\n                blocked = True\n            for p in targets:\n                if p.get('state') == 'recorded':\n                    messages.append('A recorded promise cannot be changed here; direct changes to the mobile app.')\n                    blocked = True\n                else:\n                    p['state'] = 'note'\n                    p['reason'] = event\n                    if event == 'paid':\n                        messages.append('Explain that payments can take one business day to appear.')\n            vars['split_started'] = 'yes'\n        elif event in ['refuse', 'too_much']:\n            vars['split_started'] = 'yes'\n            if not targets:\n                messages.append('Clarify which actual product this concerns.')\n                blocked = True\n            else:\n                p = targets[0]\n                if p.get('state') == 'recorded':\n                    messages.append('A recorded promise cannot be changed here; direct changes to the mobile app.')\n                    blocked = True\n                elif vars.get('hardship_active') == 'yes':\n                    messages.append('Offer connection to support; make no persuasion attempt.')\n                    blocked = True\n                else:\n                    p['state'] = 'open'\n                    if event == 'too_much':\n                        p['full_too_much'] = True\n                    if event == 'too_much' and not p.get('floor_offered'):\n                        p['floor_offered'] = True\n                        if initial_offer:\n                            text = offer(p)\n                        else:\n                            p['offer_amount'] = p['floor']\n                            p['amount'] = p['floor']\n                            text = 'Offer the floor of ' + str(p['floor']) + ' for ' + p['label'] + (' on ' + str(p.get('offer_date')) if p.get('offer_date') else '') + ' once. Explain that the rest stays overdue. Obtain agreement; do not ask how much they can pay.'\n                    else:\n                        p.setdefault('rejected', []).append(signature(p.get('offer_amount', p['past_due']), p.get('offer_date', '')))\n                        text = offer(p)\n                    if text:\n                        messages.append(text)\n                        blocked = True\n        elif event in ['accept', 'proposal', 'correction']:\n            vars['split_started'] = 'yes'\n            if not targets:\n                messages.append('Clarify which actual product is meant.')\n                blocked = True\n            if amount_text and len(targets) > 1 and amount_scope != 'per_product':\n                messages.append('You proposed an amount for several products. Clarify which product that amount concerns; do not allocate it or copy a combined total to each product.')\n                blocked = True\n                targets = []\n            for p in targets:\n                if p.get('state') == 'recorded':\n                    messages.append('The promise for ' + p['label'] + ' is already recorded and cannot be changed or cancelled here. Direct changes to the mobile app.')\n                    blocked = True\n                    continue\n                old_date = p.get('date', '')\n                p['state'] = 'open'\n                p['date'] = ''\n                a = float(amount_text) if amount_text else float(p.get('offer_amount', p['past_due']) if event == 'ac